## Purpose

Preserve the Prime Agent architecture discussion in-repository before returning to PR #149.

This is a **research/documentation-only Draft PR**. It does not change production code, does not alter the accepted canonical `ROADMAP.md`, and does not authorize Prime integration.

The preserved research set now contains:

- `project-context/PRIME_RUNTIME_ADAPTATION_ROADMAP.md` — the staged Prime research/adaptation roadmap;
- `project-context/PRIME_RUNTIME_ADAPTATION_ROADMAP_ADDENDUM.md` — the execution details that were not explicit enough in the first draft and must be folded into the roadmap after #149.

Together they record:

- persistent rich-context ChatGPT conversations as the default reasoning path;
- Temporary Chat as a specialized independent-review profile, not the universal Agent Session model;
- ordinary ChatGPT Plus / GPT-5.6 Sol as the intended actual reasoning source;
- Prime as a candidate session/runtime substrate rather than CAP authority;
- CAP retaining identity, authorization, ambiguity handling, provenance, effect execution, Verification Kernel and Finish Gate;
- one narrow Prime adapter/custom `streamSimple` provider with no implicit external-model fallback;
- the resumable `NEEDS_MODEL / WAITING_FOR_CHATGPT -> MODEL_RESPONSE -> Prime resumes` boundary, avoiding recursive same-turn deadlock;
- candidate `procedure_run` continuation operations without adding a new public ChatGPT tool;
- a durable one-Prime-session <-> one-persistent-ChatGPT-conversation binding, including explicit replacement/recovery semantics;
- automatic browser wake plus explicit CAP/plugin invocation and qualification prerequisites;
- exactly-once/no-blind-duplicate model-turn delivery and crash recovery;
- deterministic-vs-intelligence-required scheduler wake separation;
- zero Codex / zero Work-agent execution / zero external LLM API qualification;
- exact Prime version/commit/configuration pinning and requalification instead of blind upstream auto-updates;
- AgentSession/retained-worker validation as the core proof of Prime's persistent-runtime value before using an ephemeral reviewer as a later product consumer;
- Anthropic `commerce-agents` as a required mechanism reference for the later Prime Stage Research at the `Prime rich context -> CAP authority/effects` boundary, especially object/observation provenance, untrusted-content fencing, staged consequence boundaries and outcome-oriented regression design; all material claims must be re-traced to an exact upstream ref under `source-code-research` before adoption;
- A/B evaluation including maintenance/dependency cost and explicit `ADAPT | KEEP | ADOPT` decision gates;
- messaging/goals/scheduler/subagents/memory deferred until the core bridge/session/trust gates pass.

## Sequencing

This branch is intentionally based on the currently accepted `main`. Work order is:

1. park this Prime research branch;
2. return to and finish PR #149;
3. merge #149 after its required gates;
4. refresh this branch from the new `main`;
5. rerun repository skill bootstrap;
6. fold the addendum into the main Prime roadmap;
7. perform exact-source Prime Stage Research under `stage-research` + `source-code-research`, including the Anthropic Commerce Agents mechanism reference at an exact pinned ref;
8. implement only after a `PROCEED` or `NARROW` decision.

## Post-#149 decision gate

Do **not** implement a broad generic existing-session runtime immediately after PR #149. First use exact-source Prime Stage Research to determine the CAP/Prime ownership boundary, because Prime is explicitly being evaluated as a possible substrate for session runtime, persistence, supervision, attach/detach, retained workers and related messaging/runtime mechanics.

Required order after #149 is accepted and merged:

```text
#149 accepted + merged
        ↓
refresh Prime #151 from new main
        ↓
exact-source Prime Stage Research
        ↓
determine CAP / Prime ownership boundary
        ↓
ADAPT | KEEP | ADOPT
        ↓
separate Existing-Session Delivery Stage Research
        ↓
implement only the CAP-owned remainder
```

Prime may own, if Stage Research and evidence support it:

- session runtime;
- persistence;
- supervisor/daemon mechanics;
- attach/detach;
- retained sessions/workers;
- messaging/runtime mechanics that do not become CAP authority.

CAP must retain unless separately researched and accepted otherwise:

- opaque target / ChatGPT conversation binding and exact target identity;
- stable `delivery_id` / `model_request_id` identity;
- one-shot physical Send authority;
- ambiguous outcome -> `unknown` handling and reconciliation;
- no blind resend;
- wrong/foreign conversation rejection;
- durable delivery receipt / exact delivery correlation;
- source/runtime provenance;
- capability/authorization boundary;
- verification and Finish Gate authority.

The generic existing-session capability must remain consumer-neutral. MimiSeek, automatic reviewer continuation, Prime model requests and later manager wake/resumption are consumers of the same generic session/delivery primitive. CAP must not gain MimiSeek-, UV Studio-, GitHub-, repository-, PR-, review-, `PASS`- or `FINDINGS`-specific routing or semantics.

The later Prime Stage Research must additionally answer, without preselecting a new framework:

- whether CAP needs first-class provenance for object/observation references crossing from persistent Prime/ChatGPT context into consequence-bearing effects;
- how trusted instructions/authoritative state remain distinguishable from untrusted external observations and worker/page/message content in long-lived context;
- whether any consequence class needs an explicit `propose/stage -> approve -> revalidate -> apply` boundary beyond the existing CAP `authorize -> act -> re-observe -> verify` contract;
- whether outcome/snapshot regression cases with long, messy or contradictory histories materially improve evaluation of the persistent Prime path;
- whether provenance/freshness survives compaction or context projection without allowing summaries to replace authoritative CAP facts.

Anthropic terminology is not imported as CAP authority. Names such as `GroundedReference` or `UntrustedObservation`, if ever proposed, are CAP design candidates only; the Stage Research must derive the minimum mechanism from exact source evidence and current CAP guarantees.

This decision gate is deliberately recorded in PR metadata now so it survives while the Prime branch remains parked. When #151 is refreshed after #149, this must be folded into the in-repository Prime roadmap/addendum and, if Stage Research confirms the sequencing, into the canonical roadmap before production implementation.

No Prime production implementation belongs in this PR yet.
